        {
          "lines": [
            1,
            33
          ],
          "text": "# Character family brief\n\nOwner instruction, recorded 2026-11-15 (UTC) from the project owner's request to PIXL.\n\n## Assignment\n\nMake a character family for a side-view game. The family has two members: a scout and a medic.\n\n## Owner-chosen constraints (confirmed by the owner)\n\n1. Outline: the reference's dark outline (the continuous dark outline seen in reference.png).\n2. Canvas: 32 by 32 pixels per character.\n3. Palette: the agreed teal and cream palette.\n4. Transparency: binary (each pixel fully opaque or fully transparent).\n5. View: side view.\n6. Display: nearest-neighbor sampling.\n\n## References supplied by the owner\n\n- reference.png: style reference with the dark outline (the outline treatment the owner chose).\n- reference-b.png: same figure without the outline; palette and silhouette reference only.\n\n## Authorization\n\nThe owner authorized PIXL to proceed with the choices above and to make the progress\npossible in this session. This is an isolated evaluation project: no package installs,\nno network, no generation provider is assigned, and only the local PIXL MCP is configured.\n\n## Left open by the owner\n\n- Exact destination paths for delivered files in the game project.\n- Intended display scale of the game.\n- Poses, animation and how the scout and medic are told apart beyond their names.\n"
        }
      ],
      "scope": "Exact cited text only; its meaning and support for the criterion need caller comparison.",
